<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 23 July, from 1637 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1637</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Riot greets Charles I's new prayer book in Edinburgh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Worshippers in St Giles' Cathedral protested violently when the new Scottish Book of Common Prayer was first read. The resistance led to the National Covenant, the Bishops' Wars and the British civil wars.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1745</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bonnie Prince Charlie lands on Eriskay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Edward Stuart landed on the Hebridean island of Eriskay to reclaim the throne for his father. The Jacobite rising he launched ended in defeat at Culloden in April 1746.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1829</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Austin Burt patents his 'typographer'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Michigan surveyor William Austin Burt received a US patent for the typographer, a hand-operated printing machine. Slow and never sold commercially, it is often called the first American typewriter.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1952</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt's Free Officers overthrow King Farouk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers led by Muhammad Naguib and Gamal Abdel Nasser seized power in a bloodless coup, forcing King Farouk to abdicate days later. Egypt became a republic in 1953.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1974</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greece's military junta collapses after the Cyprus crisis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Discredited by its coup in Cyprus and the Turkish invasion that followed, the Greek junta handed power to civilians. Konstantinos Karamanlis returned from exile the next day to restore democracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></li></ol>
